    "question": "Tom and Devin have been teaching for a total of 70 years. Devin has been teaching for 5 less than half the number of years that Tom has. How many years has Tom been teaching?",
    "gold": "50",
    "answer": "Let x be the number of years Tom has been teaching\nDevin has been teaching for (1/2)x-5 years\n70=x+((1/2)x-5)\n70=(3/2)x-5\n75=(3/2)x\nx=<<50=50>>50\nTom has been teaching for 50 years\n#### 50"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "Let T be the number of years Tom has been teaching and D be the number of years Devin has been teaching. We know that T + D = 70 and D = 1/2T - 5.\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get T + 1/2T - 5 = 70.\nCombining like terms, we get 1.5T - 5 = 70.\nAdding 5 to both sides, we get 1.5T = 75.\nDividing both sides by 1.5, we get T = 50.\nThe final answer is \\boxed{50}.",
